IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Row il-57. NOUNS of a cross-reference and of a pronoun in replacement words. No rule is written here; the facts below are what a reader of the texts could state.
-- TARGET COMPILER: main. No REFUSE, no section GIVEN, no TYPICALLY, no YMD, no sets: a case the sources do not answer is NOTHING from a MAYBE.
--
-- This row is NOT an encoding of the Women's Employment Law, 5714-1954 ("the Law"). It records three things that the printed texts show, each with one sound control beside it.
-- (1) A list of extensions: section 6(ב)(2) defines a term by listing three subsections; Amendment 67 added a fourth extension to the Law and to the rule that counts the extensions, but not to that list.
-- (2) A list of subsections: section 51(ד) of the National Insurance Law names the payment date for the additional maternity allowance of two subsections; Amendment 67 added a third subsection that gives it.
-- (3) A pronoun: five days of unpaid leave are added to a paragraph about "עובד או עובדת" with the words "שהיא הוצאה", a feminine form.
-- A citation whose two descriptions differ, a list that leaves out a member the Law has, or a pronoun that does not fit a noun the paragraph names, is a defect, and is kept in an expected-red file.
--
-- THE KINDS BELOW ARE MINE, not the Law's: each is a short plain description I wrote from reading the citing words and the target, so that two descriptions of the same thing are the same kind.
-- The words of the texts are quoted beside each value in the references module (`src:` lines are the Law's consolidation, `ext:[ni]` lines are the National Insurance Law's consolidation,
-- `ext:[SH ...]` lines are typed from a page image of the official instrument).

§ `Nouns of a cross-reference`

DECLARE `What a provision is about` IS ONE OF
    `the extensions under sections 6(ב1), (ג) and (ד) of the Law`
    `the extensions under sections 6(ב1), (ג), (ד) and (ד3) of the Law`
    `section 6(ד3) of the Law as Amendment 67 inserts it`
    `the payment date of the additional maternity allowance under section 51(א) and (א1) of the National Insurance Law`
    `the payment date of the additional maternity allowance under section 51(א), (א1) and (א3) of the National Insurance Law`
    `the rules of sections 6(ב), (ג) and (ד) of the Law`
    `the rules of the sections of the Law that section 9ג(ב) lists`

-- Three kinds of reading, from the strongest to the weakest.
-- The second kind is the honest name for most limbs (b) here: the official page was read, but that no LATER instrument touched the words rests on the consolidation.
DECLARE `Where a reading comes from` IS ONE OF
    `the official instrument, read from its page image`
    `the official instrument, read from its page image; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
    `the consolidation only`

DECLARE `A cross-reference` HAS
    `the citing words are in` IS A STRING
    `the citing words say it points at` IS A `What a provision is about`
    `the target is` IS A `What a provision is about`
    `the subsection the amending instrument added` IS A STRING
    `the citing words name that subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amending instrument takes effect on` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `limb (a) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
    `limb (b) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

§ `Nouns of a pronoun in replacement words`

DECLARE `Grammatical gender` IS ONE OF
    `masculine`
    `feminine`

DECLARE `A pronoun in replacement words` HAS
    `the replacement words are in` IS A STRING
    `the nouns the head of the paragraph names` IS A LIST OF `Grammatical gender`
    `the gender of the pronoun and its verb` IS A `Grammatical gender`
    `limb (a) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
    `limb (b) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
